      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOn `main`, the default attention backend on ROCm is `aiter`, which has no RDNA (gfx11xx / gfx120x) kernels. An RDNA server with default flags therefore never comes up.\n\n**Without aiter installed** (the normal setup on Radeon), the first decode CUDA graph capture fails:\n\n```\nFile \".../layers/attention/aiter_backend.py\", line 2023, in init_forward_metadata_out_graph\nNameError: name 'reset_verify_attn_plan_cache' is not defined\n```\n\n**Passing `--attention-backend triton` is not enough either.** The Triton backend's Lean decode auto-gate turns Lean on, and its kernel needs more LDS than RDNA's 64 KiB:\n\n```\ntriton.runtime.errors.OutOfResources: out of resource: shared memory, Required: 66560, Hardware limit: 65536.\n```\n\n`amd_march` fixed both in #42092 (merged): consumer RDNA defaults to Triton attention, and Lean's auto-gate stays off there unless requested explicitly. This PR ports that change to `main`, together with the `is_rdna` platform fact it relies on, which came from `amd_march`'s multi-arch work. Related: #36867 targets the same symptom with an aiter architecture allowlist. That list doesn't include gfx1250, so it would also move gfx1250 off aiter. This port only touches gfx11xx / gfx120x. #46912 is an alternative fix for the Lean LDS overflow (smaller tile); the two don't conflict. Context: #46900.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `utils/common.py`: add `is_rdna_supported()` (gfx11xx and gfx120x; excludes gfx1250), identical to `amd_march`'s.\n- `runtime_context.py`: expose it as the platform fact `is_rdna`.\n- `model_override_base.py`: in the MHA branch on HIP, return `triton` when `is_rdna`, else `aiter` as before.\n- `triton_backend.py`: when `enable_lean_attention` is unset (auto) on RDNA, use the standard decode kernel. An explicit `True` still enables Lean for bring-up.\n\nCDNA is unchanged. On gfx950 (MI355X), `get_platform().is_rdna` is `False`, so the default stays `aiter` and Lean's auto-gate is untouched. `test_platform_context.py` passes (8/8).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nRDNA4 (gfx1201), stock `rocm/pytorch:rocm7.2.3_ubuntu24.04_py3.12_pytorch_release_2.10.0`, no aiter, default server flags. Both arms use the same base:\n\n- `main` (58214f648c)\n- #43679, so sgl-kernel builds for gfx1201\n- a local guard making the quark aiter imports optional, so `import sglang` works without aiter; that is what #40863 / #46914 do\n\nQwen/Qwen3-8B and allenai/OLMoE-1B-7B-0125-Instruct. `sgl-eval==0.1.2` gsm8k, `enable_thinking=false`, temperature 0.7, top_p 0.8.\n\n| | base | base + this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Qwen3-8B server | ❌ `NameError: name 'reset_verify_attn_plan_cache' is not defined` | ✅ up in 45 s, decode CUDA graphs captured |\n| Qwen3-8B gsm8k (100 questions) | — | 94% |\n| Qwen3-8B `bench_serving` random-ids 512/256, c=1 / c=8 | — | 24.9 / 188.8 tok/s (median TPOT 39.9 / 40.8 ms) |\n| OLMoE-1B-7B server | ❌ same `NameError` | ✅ up in 35 s |\n| OLMoE gsm8k (50 questions) | — | 62% |\n\nThe same change has been on `amd_march` since #42092. Our daily RDNA job on `amd_march` (with the open RDNA fixes) gets the same results ([run](https://github.com/vivienfanghuagood/sglang/actions/runs/40852621154)).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThe numbers above are for RDNA only. CDNA selection is unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (Port of a merged `amd_march` change. The platform-probe test covers the new fact; happy to add a backend-selection test if wanted.)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No doc change needed.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results. (See above.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40886039959](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40886039959)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40886039899](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40886039899)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40886039553](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40886039553)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
